Part C: the regime split is governed by the SMALL part's own loneliness M(P)
==================================================================================
  In regime B, the small part P=S∩{1..13} is ALREADY lonely (M(P)>=1/14) at a
  small-small crossing that the cluster does not spoil -> private-q irrelevant.
  In regime A, M(P) is spoiled by the cluster and the (flank,w) crossing decides.
  regime A (M-binding big > 13 and privately owns q): 137
  regime B (otherwise; small or non-private big):      360
